// =============================================================================
//  probe_affinity.hml — acceptance probe for src/sim/affinity.hml and for the
//  affinity APPLICATION in src/sim/combat.hml.
// =============================================================================
//
//  Run it FROM THE NIGHTSHADE REPO ROOT, and BOTH ways:
//
//      hemlockc -O1 tools/probe_affinity.hml -o /tmp/paf && /tmp/paf
//      hemlock  tools/probe_affinity.hml
//
//  It exits 1 on any failure AND on an assertion-COUNT mismatch.
//
//  THE ONE ASSERTION THAT MATTERS MOST is section G.  The brief says the
//  affinity axis "must not break the measured TTK tables for neutral enemies —
//  verify the unaffected cases still reproduce exactly", and section G does not
//  verify that approximately.  It runs every shipped class against every
//  pre-spell-school delivery kind against a table of awkward f64 damage values,
//  and compares the HP removed against a REFERENCE IMPLEMENTATION OF THE
//  PRE-AFFINITY FUNCTION BODY transcribed into this file.  432 cases, zero
//  tolerance, integer equality.  Plus F7/F8, which assert the underlying reason
//  it can be zero-tolerance: `x * 1.0` is exact in IEEE-754.
//
//  WHY THE GLOAM AND THE SNUFFER CAN BE TESTED AT ALL.  `config.hml` still says
//  `g_ENEMY_KIND_COUNT = 6` and widening it is not this task's file to own, so
//  neither class can SPAWN.  But `world.model` is an ordinary i32 column and
//  `combat_apply_damage` is reachable directly, so classes 6 and 7 are exercised
//  by writing the model index by hand.  That is a real test of the arithmetic
//  and it is NOT a test that the classes exist — see the task report, which
//  states plainly which halves of those two rows are unbuilt.
// =============================================================================

